 "_about": "Layer 2 (product line) and layer 3 (series) of Cisco switches, operator's model 14 Sep 2026. SKU patterns first (a SKU family token wins over a wrong series label), then names, then the stored series labels for rows with no family token (cords, kits). SKUs are upper-cased with a trailing '=' removed before matching. A spare, a power supply or a fan of a series sits IN that series; its part type stays underneath. Reviewer review 14 Sep 2026 applied: series carry `role` (the one series->deploy_role table, read by src/core/deployRole.ts); generic accessories (cords, generic cables, rack kits, blanks, console cables) whose SKU does not name a series go to '<line> shared parts' (shared_accessories); Small Business (SF/SG/SX) and Cisco Business (CBS) are separate lines by generation.",
